      "message": "Tethering.apk is an older APK inside the Connectivity APEX, which is separate from service-connectivity. Basically inside the module there is:\n\n    /apex/com.android.tethering/javalib/service-connectivity.jar\n    /apex/com.android.tethering/priv-app/Tethering@VERSION/Tethering.apk\n\nAt runtime they\u0027re really separate, so `new Intent(mContext.getApplicationContext(), DownloadService.class)` won\u0027t find the service (the \"application\" context of service-connectivity, which is system_server, won\u0027t find classes inside Tethering.apk, which is an app).\n\nPutting CTDownloadService code inside Tethering.apk doesn\u0027t sound right though, I think it should either run directly in system_server, or be its own app. Tethering.apk is pretty special (it has its own UID, special signature, sepolicy context) and is kind of \"legacy\" from Android R, newer stuff is built into service-connectivity.",
